# Raw and processed data — never in git, at any size (CLAUDE.md rule 4).
# The corpus is ~950MB raw plus an ~85MB processed file, and this repo is public.
data/raw/
data/processed/
# Run outputs, too: model text, per-case results, and the spec of each run — whose
# case_ids, on a held-out run, is the ordered held-out case list (CLAUDE.md rule 4, 0026).
data/runs/
# The docket cache: fetched NTSB docket listing pages and documents (PDFs, images).
# Decision 0037 permits only redacted, reviewed, NTSB-authored text in git — a cached
# docket page or document is neither redacted nor reviewed, and this repo is public.
data/docket/
# The local hand-check marking page (scripts/handcheck_page.py): unredacted document titles
# and links that name real cases, for the owner's own browser only. Decision 0049 keeps the
# committed sheet this folds into (tests/fixtures/docket/title_handcheck.csv) redacted; this
# is that sheet's working copy, never the committed artefact.
data/handcheck/
# Whole-directory catch-all, kept alongside the specific lines above rather than replacing
# them (they document *why* each kind of file under data/ is excluded). Without this, a file
# the specific lines do not enumerate -- e.g. the recorder's data/recorder.log, or its store's
# WAL/SHM side files before the *.sqlite-wal/-shm lines below existed -- sat untracked but NOT
# git-ignored, one `git add -A` away from landing open-split text in this public repository
# (S2.5 Task 10, fix round 1, Important 4). "Nothing under data/ is committed" (CLAUDE.md rule
# 4) is enforced here as a rule, not only as a list of known cases.
# Anchored to the repo root (S2.5 Task 10, fix round 3, Important): an unqualified "data/"
# matches at ANY depth, not only the repo root -- it silently also matched the tracked package
# `src/ntsb_probable_cause/data/`, which meant every file in that package was untracked-and-
# ignored (invisible to `git status`) AND skipped entirely by `ruff check` (ruff honours
# ignore files even for tracked files), so lint stopped covering that package with nobody
# noticing. The leading slash restricts this rule to the repository root's own `data/`, which
# is the only one this rule was ever meant to reach -- the specific lines above it (`data/raw/`
# etc.) were never affected, since a pattern containing an internal slash is already anchored
# to the `.gitignore`'s own directory by git's own rules.
/data/
*.zip
*.mdb
*.accdb
*.parquet

# Secrets. The OpenRouter key and anything like it lives in the environment.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local state. The predictions store is derived and rebuildable; the committed
# ledger is the durable, tamper-evident record.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
# SQLite's own WAL-mode side files (store/db.py opens every store with journal_mode=WAL) and
# the older rollback-journal mode's file -- these hold uncommitted or since-checkpointed page
# data, which for the recorder's store is open-split text (CLAUDE.md rule 5). *.sqlite above
# already covers the main file; these cover it mid-write, wherever a store lives.
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-journal

# Account-specific operational values, referenced from docs/runbooks/.
*.local.md

# Build and tooling output
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
cdk.out/
dist/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
.claude/worktrees/

# There is no config.yaml (decision 0012): field roles, splits and API facts are
# typed constants in the library, and per-run values come from the environment.
# The spike ignored its config and its filled labelling sheets, which is why its
# headline numbers once rested on files nobody else could open. Everything a number
# depends on is tracked here; only secrets stay in the environment.
